WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:09.420
Mobile Suit Gundam 0083

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.810
What?! Commandant Giren
has been killed in action?!

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.510
Yes, sir! Lady Kycilia now
has command of all of A Baoa Qu!

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.280
You planned this all along,
didn't you, Kycilia!

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.020
You Feddie cannon fodder!

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.460
Recall all ships
and mobile suits!

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.340
Our fleet is retreating
from this sector!

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.210
Lieutenant, stop!
They've issued orders to retreat!

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.150
Gato, wait!

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.090
Your ship, the carrier <i>Doroa,</i>
has been destroyed!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.490
The <i>Doroa?!</i>

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.750
And our Commander-in-Chief,
Giren, has also been lost.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:13.630
We're retreating
from A Baoa Qu.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.130
We must live on to carry
on the will of our leader!

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.400
You mean live on in shame?!
I'm going out!

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.870
No!

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:29.810
For now, you must endure. Until
the day we can regain our glory...

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:34.180
...you must put your life
in my hands! Is that clear?

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.350
It was the greatest
battle of the One Year War.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.150
After the Battle of A Baoa Qu,
an armistice was signed between...

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.940
...the Earth Federation government
and the Republic of Zeon.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.260
But the seeds of another
battle had already been sown.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:00.450
GUNDAMJACK

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.310
This god damned Zaku!
It maneuvers like a pig!

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.450
There's no way it can
compare to that powered up GM!

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.450
<i>Kou! Keith! Formation 3!</i>
<i>Let's hit him all at once!</i>

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.090
- Roger!
- <i>Roger!</i>

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.860
All right!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.950
Have you been studying your piloting
like you should, Ensign Keith?

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.180
I've gotcha!

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.630
Shit! That thing's
thrust is incredible!

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.980
That backpack's
too heavy for a GM.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.380
I bet it'd look a
lot better on a Zaku.

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.380
<i>Keith! Stay on the GM's tail!</i>

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.360
<i>Drive him toward the ruins ahead!</i>
<i>I'll head him off there!</i>

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:58.450
Huh? Like I can actually
keep up with that thing?

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.400
It... It's too fast!

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.080
Oh, this is NOT happening!

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.620
Lt. Burning, Keith's unit is
trapped in the rubble and can't move.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.430
He's going to need a pickup.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.020
Mm. Keith, just sit tight.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.400
We'll send someone
to get you out later.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.960
<i>Roger...</i>

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.460
Lt. Burning, we don't have all
the data on the GM's jet pack yet.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.170
They still haven't pushed it
to its maximum thrust rating.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.180
Right. Lt. Allen,
this is Burning.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.270
Continue maneuvers with the
jet pack at full thrust.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.680
<i>Roger!</i>

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.210
Mr. Paserov. All quiet?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.490
Excuse me for coming up here
without permission, Capt. Synapse.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.790
It's no bother, Miss Purpleton.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.490
But there's been nothing
but ocean since we left Jaburo.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.160
Aren't you bored?

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.130
Not at all. It may be
the same ocean, but...

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:48.540
...the waves' movement and color
changes from place to place.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:54.140
Oh, of course. This is your first
time down here on Earth, isn't it?

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.870
Yes.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.510
We'll be over
Australia soon, won't we?

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.110
We already are.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:05.520
We're already
crossing over Sydney.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:09.150
The sea we're over now
is where the city used to be.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:12.180
The scar of the Zeons'
Operation British.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.140
This... This is where
the colony fell?!

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.770
A crater 500 kilometers wide.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.470
The largest man
made hole in history...

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.210
...created by an explosive force
equal to 60,000 megatons.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.180
They may call it the cost of war,
but it's too high a price to pay.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.520
Commander Gato, it's here.
The Pegasus-class ship.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:53.500
Right on schedule. The captain's
quite punctual for a Feddie.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.100
- Looks that way.
- Contact the Jukon!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.800
Yes, sir!

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.780
This is Walfisch.
Pegasus-class sighted.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.510
Now commencing
Operation Stardust.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.080
92...

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.090
93...

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.450
94...

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.750
95...

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.450
96...

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.480
What's that?

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:20.160
Is something scheduled
to come in today?

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:24.000
Hm, looks like Jaburo's got
a lot of money to play with.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.500
Wish they'd send a
little of it our way.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.200
Is that? Is that a
Pegasus-class, Lieutenant?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.010
If that's an improved
version of <i>White Base...</i>

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.740
Do you think they have any
Gundam-type suits on board?!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:41.770
All right! When do we get
to see them, Lieutenant?!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.790
Whoa, now hold on.
You'll get all the details.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.690
Just wait till the
briefing tomorrow morning.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.850
Good work today. Dismissed.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.850
Keith! You gonna
lie there all day?!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.870
Y... Yes, sir...

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.510
Keith, it's landing.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:22.750
It's incredible!

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.760
Yeah, incredible!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.190
All right, that settles it!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.500
Hey, Kou! Not so fast! Kou!

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.130
You know, I love how
hanging around with you...

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.470
...gets me into the
most wonderful accidents.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.840
Of course.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:46.750
So, where are we going,
my dear Kou?

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:48.510
To pay them a visit.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:50.640
You don't mean?!

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.180
You bet I mean it.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:58.180
Honestly, I'll never be
bored hanging around with you.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.450
Reporting, sir. Capt. Synapse
and the 211 crew members of...

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.450
...the assault carrier <i>Albion</i>
are here on schedule...

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.450
...with the two new
prototype mobile suits.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.420
Well done, Captain.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.360
General Marnery, I know
this is a bit sudden...

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.720
...but I'd like to open the
nuclear weapon storage bunker.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.730
Here's the
authorization from Jaburo...

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.820
...and the test schedule
we'll be starting tomorrow.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.130
Hm... I'll leave it to
you to choose a test pilot.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.470
The files are all ready.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:44.470
Do a good job.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:45.670
I'll do my best, sir.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.740
So, it IS a Gundam...

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.080
Whoa! Kou! Hey, Kou!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.170
- What?
- Look!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.480
TWO Gundams!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.420
Keith, check this out!
This one's got a core fighter!

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:40.990
I'm not blind, you know.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.970
That's one's great, too!
That heavy armor!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.430
It's something else!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.730
Yeah, she's something else,
all right.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.470
Are you from the base?

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:53.410
And you?
Anaheim Electronics, right?

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.100
Y- Yes...

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:58.710
We... Uh, I mean I'm Ensign Chuck
Keith, a test pilot here.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.440
Oh, you're a test pilot.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:05.440
I'm Nina Purpleton, systems
engineer. It's a pleasure.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.460
Believe me,
the pleasure's all mine.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.120
Oh, that's my pal,
Ensign Kou Uraki.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.860
Kou, this is Nina. Kou!

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.150
Yeah? What?

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:19.460
This is Nina. She's a
systems engineer with Anaheim.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.130
Oh. Hi.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.040
He's shy, especially
around beautiful women.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.940
Just beautiful women?

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.450
The Gundam's being
serviced right now.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.680
If you want to see it,
you'll be contacted tomorrow.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:34.620
Then you can contact me.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.710
Huh?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.080
- When do you get off work today?
- What?

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:42.060
Well, we have to set a
time for our date, don't we?

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.460
Wanna grab a beer?

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:44.620
Nina!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.130
What, Orville?

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.130
Everything checks out O.K.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.460
If you don't need me,
I'd like to take a walk.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.470
Sure thing. Good work.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.630
Take a walk? But there's
nothing around here.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.970
Perhaps, but everything
here on Earth...

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.870
...is new to people like
us who were born in space.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:04.410
Oh, yes. Sunsets! I guess
he went to see one of those.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.420
It should be
time for it, right?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.710
I can take you to the best
place to watch a sunset.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.310
No, thanks. I'm not
that desperate to see it.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.160
Not now, Kou.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.460
I said not now.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.830
Dammit, Kou, you...

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.060
Nobody likes a guy who
comes on too strong, kid.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.730
Duh... Duh...

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.100
A date? Be glad to!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.600
Especially since you don't seem
to want to let go of my fingers.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.130
We can do the sunset
or grab a beer.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.320
Should be about an hour from here.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:58.120
Blau Engel to Walfisch.
Blau Engel to Walfisch.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.070
<i>This is Walfisch.</i>

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:03.440
Blau Engel is ready.
Everything is on schedule.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.070
<i>Walfisch, roger.</i>

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:00.020
This is the first time
we've opened it...

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.090
...since the Antarctic
Treaty was signed.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:06.470
If I could, I'd make sure that
door stayed closed forever.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.440
I don't want you
being careless, Lt. Bob.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.070
It may be a backwater base...

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.950
...but test pilots can be
among the most skilled.

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:23.420
Leave it to us, sir.

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.910
You're the linchpin here,
Commander. Be careful.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.090
Your name's Orville, right?

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.360
Could you only find a
lieutenant's uniform for me?

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.950
Sorry, Commander.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.900
Well, it doesn't
change who I really am.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.130
I expect only the best from you.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:55.950
That backpack we mounted on
the GM has incredible output!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.980
And the shock absorbers
on the legs...

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.350
...let it handle long
falls without any problems.

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:03.360
If it's that good on a GM, I can't
wait to try it on the new suits.

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:06.990
What do you mean YOU can't wait
to try it on the new suits?!

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:11.360
Allen, I told you the pilot of
the new unit hasn't been chosen yet.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.360
C'mon, Lieutenant, you and I
are the ace pilots here...

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.870
...so I figured
it was a no-brainer.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.640
I wanna try one, too!
Day after day...

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.740
...all I get to
drive is that stupid Zaku!

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.270
Oh, but the Zaku's
a fine machine, too.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.650
And who the hell are you?!

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:32.950
Pardon me. I'm a systems engineer
with Anaheim. Nina Purpleton.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:37.120
Oh, with Anaheim, huh?
Pardon my man's rudeness.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.790
I'm Lt. Burning, the chief
test pilot instructor here.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.990
Karcs!

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:45.500
- 'Scuse me, ma'am!
- Forget it.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.800
Lieutenant, this is
Lieutenant j.g. Mora Bascht.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.930
She came here from Jaburo to
oversee the maintenance team.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:54.840
Hope you won't be too
hard on me, Lieutenant, sir!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.940
Um, do you boys
mind if we joined you?

00:15:57.980 --> 00:15:59.380
By all means.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.620
Looks like you've really upped
the power on that new equipment.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.950
You've already tested
the new backpack?

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:09.960
We mounted it on
a souped-up GM today.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.960
It increased the power incredibly.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.990
By the way, we've heard
you'll be choosing...

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.330
...test pilots from this
base for those new suits.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.560
May I ask what kind of pilots
you'd be looking for?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.530
Well, my company
would like a pilot...

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:27.700
...who can push the new suits to
the limits of their abilities, so...

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.640
Mora, we'd better get back.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:33.910
It's time already?

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.350
Gentlemen, if you'll excuse us.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.850
Excuse us, guys.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.290
What were you about to say?!

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:41.260
Hm? Oh, nothing.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.820
I'd just be worried that someone
who's just trained on old suits...

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.990
...wouldn't be able to tap the
potential of the prototypes.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.360
Down, boy.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.700
No carrots, please.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:54.860
You think so?

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.330
Um, do you have a second?

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:01.340
If you want to see it,
you can wait till tomorrow.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:04.840
The Gundam's reaction time
has been upped by 0.5 seconds...

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:06.940
...and its output increased by 30%.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:10.280
Although we didn't see
even two-thirds of that on the GM...

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:13.850
Tell me, that heavily armored
one is an anti-nuke unit...

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:16.120
...and that shoulder bazooka can
mount a tactical nuke, can't it?

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.860
I thought so!
Just wanted to make sure.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:24.660
You're a pilot, too? That was
a pretty sharp observation.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:27.360
But how sharp is his piloting?

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.040
Halt!

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:41.840
Sorry I'm so late!
Orville, from Anaheim Electronics!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.150
Right. So, how was the sunset?

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:48.320
It was outstanding.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.880
Sunrises are nice, too.

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.690
Then I'd better get
to bed early tonight.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.690
Commander, it's safe now.

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:04.670
Lax security, isn't it?

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.700
It's like this everywhere
in the Federation.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.970
These are the
people we're fighting?

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:46.920
Setup, complete.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.180
Now we can relax a little.

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.810
You'll be very busy starting
tomorrow, Miss Purpleton.

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:53.650
Do your best.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.020
Yes, sir.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.530
Huh? Looks like
they're doing something.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.640
You two, down there!
This area's off-limits!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.810
- Nina?
- Uh, yes?

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.280
Should we just load the
vulcan ammo into Unit 1?

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.940
Right. Please.

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:24.680
Okay.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.480
Are you loading the
warhead into it now?

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:33.690
Yes, we are! So quit getting
in our way and get out!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.940
If she just lost the bad
attitude, she'd be perfect.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.930
Give it up, Keith. It's pretty
clear she isn't interested.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:49.270
I can see that. Let's go.
Let's go and drown my sorrows.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.800
Wait, we can still
stay a little longer.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:52.340
Forget it.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:59.090
- I'm truly heartbroken!
- All right, all right!

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.860
Magnificent.
It's a superb mobile suit.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.490
I think so, too, sir.

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:14.870
Have they finished loading the
bazooka's warhead, Ensign?

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.370
Uh, yes, sir!

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:18.530
Then I'll check it out.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:33.490
For heaven's sake! Now what
are those two up to?

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:34.750
Would you...

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:41.890
What are you doing?! Shut that
hatch and get down from there!

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.470
Who the hell?!

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.660
What's up?

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:49.690
Something's wrong.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.710
Get out of there! Do you hear me?!
Get out of there right now!

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:02.120
Somebody!
Somebody, stop Unit 2!

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:06.020
What the? Kou, wait!

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.920
Ensign Uraki?!

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:20.530
Ensign Uraki, we'll call for help!
You can't do this!

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.230
I'm a pilot, too!

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:25.240
We're still loading the ammo!
You can't take it out yet!

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:26.940
Try to hurry!

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.940
I don't believe this...

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:37.740
You, the pilot in Unit 2.
I know you can hear me.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:41.350
If you get out now, we'll go easy
on you. Get out of Unit 2 at once!

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.790
I claim this mobile suit
and its nuclear warhead.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.930
Zeon will rise again!

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:54.600
Did he say Zeon?

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.740
Hull breach in the
port side hangar bay!

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:02.840
Confirming damage report!

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.240
Captain, we've got a report
from the hangar bay.

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:08.040
Someone claiming to be a
Zeon has taken Unit 2!

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.310
They're stealing Unit 2?!

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.910
Incoming missiles!
Altitude: 12,000!

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:14.180
What?!

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:30.430
Port side engine, hit!
Output dropping.

00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:32.440
All sections, report damage!

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:35.040
- Trace those missiles' firing point!
- Aye, sir.

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.770
Broadcast Minovsky particles!

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:38.140
Aye, sir!

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:44.420
God dammit, what the hell
are the Zeon up to now?!

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:48.420
Captain Synapse,
you have to stop Unit 1!

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:50.150
What about Unit 1?

00:22:50.190 --> 00:22:54.060
<i>That test pilot Ensign Uraki</i>
<i>is going after Unit 2 in it!</i>

00:22:58.170 --> 00:22:59.930
You got that
live ammo loaded yet?!

00:22:59.970 --> 00:23:02.400
Karcs! Keith! Move it!

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:05.130
This isn't play-fighting! Watch your
asses out there! You hear me?!

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:06.230
Aye, aye!

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:07.740
Lieutenant! It's the Zeon!

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:10.580
They just stole Unit 2,
and it's armed with a nuke!

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:13.470
- What?
- The Zeon?!

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:16.010
Do those guys
still want to fight?!

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:17.780
How many people do
they have to kill?!

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:19.620
- Let's go!
- Aye, sir!

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.430
What's that?!

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.130
A Zaku...

00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:41.410
The Feddies must have captured it.
I can't stand to see it like this!

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.070
<i>Commander Gato!</i>

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:09.300
Gaily! Mission accomplished!
Withdraw at once!

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:08.000
<i>You're not going anywhere!</i>

00:24:54.550 --> 00:24:59.590
<i>Don't come to me just 'cause you're lonely tonight...</i>

00:24:59.590 --> 00:25:04.220
<i>Lonely's only part of your game...</i>

00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:10.020
<i>As long as you live, you must remember one thing...</i>

00:25:10.020 --> 00:25:14.800
<i>Give and take are one and the same...</i>

00:25:14.800 --> 00:25:17.370
<i>So tell me are you ready?</i>

00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:20.040
<i>Really, really ready?</i>

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:24.550
<i>I don't want your love for one night!</i>

00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:30.340
<i>'Cause I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:25:30.340 --> 00:25:35.200
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near...</i>

00:25:35.540 --> 00:25:40.690
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:25:40.690 --> 00:25:45.860
<i>I need the magic when I touch your hand!</i>

00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:51.020
<i>I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:56.190
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near!</i>

00:25:56.190 --> 00:26:01.370
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:26:01.370 --> 00:26:08.820
<i>I need the magic when I touch...touch your hand...</i>

00:26:26.080 --> 00:26:27.780
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:28.030 --> 00:26:30.400
In the desolate vastness of
Australia, the deadly battle...

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:33.560
...between the Zeon remnants
and the Federal Forces continues.

00:26:33.600 --> 00:26:37.970
Thrown suddenly into real battle,
Uraki undergoes a trial by fire.

00:26:38.010 --> 00:26:41.910
Cornering Unit 2 in front
of him, Uraki sees it:

00:26:41.950 --> 00:26:44.240
The enemy pilot's awesome power.

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:48.610
ENDLESS PURSUIT
